      {
        "id": "four-primary-patterns-of-power-loss",
        "title": "Four primary patterns of power loss",
        "description": "Loss of power is the most frustrating symptom because it has so many causes. The key is identifying what OTHER symptoms accompany it.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified four primary patterns:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Power loss + Black smoke (35% of cases) → Over-fuelling. Usually MAF sensor, injectors, or EGR valve. Repair: £100-£900.",
              "Power loss + Blue smoke (20% of cases) → Oil burning. Turbo seals or piston rings. Repair: £450-£4,000+.",
              "Power loss + Rattling (15% of cases) → Timing chain stretch. Timing chain has jumped. Repair: £700-£2,700.",
              "Power loss + Engine light (25% of cases) → Sensor or actuator failure. Repair: £100-£600.",
              "Power loss + Knocking (5% of cases) → Rod bearing failure. This is critical. Repair: £800-£10,000+."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The critical rule: If loss of power is accompanied by knocking, rattling, or warning lights - stop driving and get a diagnostic immediately."
          },
          {
            "type": "label",
            "text": "Common affected vehicles & engines"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "four-primary-patterns-of-power-loss",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
