      {
        "id": "when-loss-of-power-is-an-emergency",
        "title": "⚠️ WHEN LOSS OF POWER IS AN EMERGENCY",
        "description": "Stop driving immediately if loss of power is accompanied by:",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Knocking noise (deep, rhythmic) → See Rod Bearing Failure",
              "Rattling noise (persistent) → See Timing Chain Failure",
              "Oil warning light → See Oil Warning Light",
              "Temperature gauge in red → See Engine Overheating",
              "Flashing engine light → Active misfire - See Check Engine Light"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Otherwise, loss of power is driveable but needs prompt diagnosis."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Book Emergency Diagnostic"
          },
          {
            "type": "cards",
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "What happens if you ignore it",
                "text": "The Hidden Cost: Ignoring power loss damages other components. A £200 sensor becomes a £1,000+ DPF replacement. A £1,000 timing chain becomes a £5,000 engine.",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "What happens if you ignore it The hidden cost of ignoring power loss Symptom Progression Cost Impact Power loss only Gradual performance drop £100-£300 sensor Power loss + black smoke DPF damage £100-£900 → £1,000-£3,500 Power loss + rattling Chain jumps timing £700-£2,700 → £2,500-£10,000+ Power loss + knocking Bearing fails completely £800-£1,500 → £2,500-£10,000+ Power loss + blue smoke Cat/DPF damage £450-£4,000+ → £2,000+ extra The Hidden Cost: Ignoring power loss damages other components. A £200 sensor becomes a £1,000+ DPF replacement. A £1,000 timing chain becomes a £5,000 engine."
              },
              {
                "title": "What to do next",
                "text": "Step 1: Note All Symptoms - What happens when you press the accelerator? Is there smoke? What colour? Any noises? Rattling, knocking, ticking? Any warning lights? Step 2: Quick Checks (£0-£50) - Check air filter - replace if blocked (£20-£50). Check fuel filter - replace if old (£50-£100). Check for vacuum leaks (hissing sound). Step 3: Professional Diagnostic (£50-£150) - A technician will read fault codes (ECU), check live data (MAF, fuel trims), perform boost leak test (turbo), test injector performance, and check compression if internal damage suspected.",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [
