                ],
                "fullText": "What to do next Three steps to diagnose power loss Step 1: Note All Symptoms - What happens when you press the accelerator? Is there smoke? What colour? Any noises? Rattling, knocking, ticking? Any warning lights? Step 2: Quick Checks (£0-£50) - Check air filter - replace if blocked (£20-£50). Check fuel filter - replace if old (£50-£100). Check for vacuum leaks (hissing sound). Step 3: Professional Diagnostic (£50-£150) - A technician will read fault codes (ECU), check live data (MAF, fuel trims), perform boost leak test (turbo), test injector performance, and check compression if internal damage suspected. Book Diagnostic"
